What comes next (Phase 6 – Step 2)

Once you confirm the frontend is displaying products, we'll continue with features that make it look like a real ecommerce application:

Build a responsive UI with a professional layout.
Add React Router (/, /cart, /orders, /login).
Implement the Add to Cart feature backed by DynamoDB.
Upload and display product images from Amazon S3.
Containerize the React frontend with Docker.
Deploy the frontend to EKS behind the same ALB using Ingress rules.

By the end of the frontend phase, users will be able to browse products, add items to their cart, and interact with a complete three-tier application running on AWS.


