Phase 6 – Step 3 (After You Complete This)

Once the navigation is working, we'll implement the Shopping Cart.

Cart data will be stored in Amazon DynamoDB (high-speed NoSQL, ideal for session/cart data).
Orders will continue to be stored in PostgreSQL RDS (relational transactional data).
Product images will be uploaded to and served from Amazon S3.
We'll then Dockerize the React frontend, push it to Amazon ECR, deploy it to Amazon EKS, and configure AWS Load Balancer Controller so a single ALB serves both:

https://<ALB-DNS>/ → React Frontend
https://<ALB-DNS>/api → Node.js Backend

At that point, your application will closely resemble the architecture of a real production ecommerce platform and provide excellent material for AWS/DevOps.

